flowchart TD
    A[UEFI firmware starts BOOTX64.EFI] --> B[efi_main in bootloader/main.c]

    B --> C[Initialize GNU-EFI library]
    C --> D[Try optional NTFS driver]
    D --> E[Find and open kernel.elf on available filesystems]

    E -->|open failed| EFail[Print error and return EFI status]
    E -->|ok| F[Read kernel.elf into memory]

    F -->|read failed| FFail[Print error and return EFI status]
    F -->|ok| G[Validate ELF64 x86_64 image]

    G -->|invalid| GFail[Print ELF load error and return]
    G -->|ok| H[Allocate physical pages for kernel LOAD segments]

    H --> I[Copy ELF segments and zero BSS]
    I --> J[Allocate boot_info at 0x90000]

    J -->|failed| JFail[Print error and return]
    J -->|ok| K[Fill boot_info magic, kernel range, RSDP]

    K --> L[Locate GOP framebuffer]
    L --> M[Store framebuffer info in boot_info]

    M --> N[Get UEFI memory map]
    N --> O[ExitBootServices retry loop]

    O -->|failed after retries| OFail[Print error and return]
    O -->|success| P[jump_to_kernel entry, boot_info in RDI]

    P --> Q[_start in kernel/arch/x86_64/entry.asm]
    Q --> R{boot_info pointer valid?}

    R -->|no| RPanic[console_panic: boot_info pointer was null]
    R -->|yes| S{boot_info magic matches?}

    S -->|no| SPanic[console_panic: boot_info magic mismatch]
    S -->|yes| T[Call kernel_main boot_info]

    T --> U{boot_info is null?}
    U -->|yes| UPanic[console_panic: kernel_main got null boot_info]
    U -->|no| V{framebuffer exists?}

    V -->|no| VHalt[cli; hlt forever]
    V -->|yes| W[console_init with framebuffer]

    W --> X[console_clear]
    X --> Y[cpu_init_tables]
    Y --> Z[interrupts_init]
    Z --> AA[timer_init]
    AA --> AB[keyboard_init]
    AB --> AC[storage_init]

    AC --> AC1[Clear storage tables]
    AC1 --> AC2[Create demo RAM disk MBR]
    AC2 --> AC3[Register rd0 block device]
    AC3 --> AC4[ATA soft reset and probe hd1]
    AC4 --> AC5[Register hd1 if found]
    AC5 --> AC6[ahci_init]
    AC6 --> AC7[Discover MBR partitions]

    AC7 --> AD[Print kernel banner and hardware info]
    AD --> AE[shell_init]
    AE --> AF[Mount first lainfs drive as S]
    AF --> AG[Run autoexec script if active drive exists]

    AG --> AH[Main shell loop]

    AH --> AI[shell_print_prompt]
    AI --> AJ[console_read_line into input_buffer]
    AJ --> AK{input empty?}

    AK -->|yes| AL[Print newline]
    AL --> AH

    AK -->|no| AM[shell_run_command]
    AM --> AN[Split command name and args]
    AN --> AO{command is drive spec?}

    AO -->|yes, mounted/present| AP[Switch current drive]
    AP --> AH

    AO -->|yes, missing| AQ[Print drive does not exist]
    AQ --> AH

    AO -->|no| AR{matches command table?}

    AR -->|no| AS[Print unknown command]
    AS --> AH

    AR -->|yes| AT[Call command handler]
    AT --> AU{handler type}

    AU -->|help/info/ticks/clear/echo/bgcolor/fgcolor| AV[Console/info command]
    AU -->|blk/part/drives/mount/mounts| AW[Storage listing or mount command]
    AU -->|mkdrive/format/ls/write/cat| AX[lainfs file command]
    AU -->|edit| AY[editor_run]
    AU -->|ahci| AZ[Print AHCI status]
    AU -->|run| BA[Run script file]

    AV --> AH
    AW --> AH
    AX --> AH
    AZ --> AH
    BA --> AH

    AY --> BB[Load file into editor buffer]
    BB --> BC[Clear screen]
    BC --> BD[Editor loop]
    BD --> BE[draw_editor]
    BE --> BF[keyboard_read_key]

    BF --> BG{key type}
    BG -->|Ctrl+S| BH[Save file and set status]
    BG -->|Esc or Ctrl+Q| BI[Disable cursor, clear screen, return]
    BG -->|Arrows| BJ[Move cursor]
    BG -->|Backspace| BK[Delete before cursor]
    BG -->|Enter| BL[Insert newline]
    BG -->|Tab| BM[Insert four spaces]
    BG -->|Char| BN[Insert character]

    BH --> BD
    BJ --> BD
    BK --> BD
    BL --> BD
    BM --> BD
    BN --> BD
    BI --> AH
